"text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"released, and every record before it has been read. Records tracked while nothing is reading wait in memory, without a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bound, for the next read, so none tracked before a delivery starts, or between two, is lost."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A read whose task is cancelled returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and takes nothing: the next read gets the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record it was waiting for, and every one after. A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Tracker\/noOp"},{"type":"text","text":" tracker’s records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One task reads at a time. The first iterator to read holds the records until its iteration"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends or the iterator is released, as it is when its task ends. An iterator that reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"meanwhile waits its turn, logging a warning as it starts to, then reads on from the next"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record; several wait in the order they came, and one whose task is cancelled while it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"waits returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":". So a delivery started right after a cancelled one has stopped, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while it is stopping, delivers every record the cancelled one didn’t read."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/trackers\/tracker\/records-swift.struct"]}],"metadata":{"title":"Tracker.Records","externalID":"s:8Trackers7TrackerV7RecordsV","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text"